<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan 28-, 91- and 182-day T-bill yields rise.</title>
<headline>Moldovan 28-, 91- and 182-day T-bill yields rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills rose to 30.69 percent annual at an auction on Tuesday from 29.32 percent at the previous auction on August 28, a National Bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The yield on 91-day T-bills rose to 32.99 percent annual from 30.19 percent at the previous auction on August 28.</p>
<p>182-day T-bills yielded 38.48 percent, compared to 38.20 percent at the previous auction on August 20.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day paper auction:</p>
<p>						Sept 3	  Aug 28</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  3.00 million lei  3.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			1.00 million	2.11 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			   1.00 million	2.11 million</p>
<p>    Yield				   30.69 pct     29.32 pct</p>
<p>    Price				   97.7 pct	97.8 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			 97.7-98.5 pct 97.8-98.5 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				Oct 3, 1996   Sept 26, 1996</p>
<p>Full details of the 91-day paper auction:</p>
<p>						Sept 3	  Aug 28</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  9.00 million lei  7.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			9.12 million	14.75 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			   9.00 million	7.00 million</p>
<p>    Yield				   32.99 pct     30.19 pct</p>
<p>    Price				   92.4 pct	93.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			 92.4-94.0 pct 92.5-94.0 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				Dec 5, 1996   Nov 28, 1996</p>
<p>Full details of the 182-day auction:</p>
<p>						Sept 3	  Aug 20</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  5.00 million lei  5.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			4.31 million	4.06 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			   4.30 million	4.06 million</p>
<p>    Yield				   38.48 pct     38.20 pct</p>
<p>    Price				   83.9 pct	84.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			 83.9-86.5 pct 84.0-86.6 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				March 6, 1997 Feb 20,1997</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
